  "id": "confluence-model",
  "term": "confluence model",
  "definition": "In cognition research, the confluence model is an account of object comparison in which the combined effect of color and shape congruency is expected to emerge only after the separate congruency effects for each feature. In the cited EEG context, this timing pattern is expected regardless of task.",
